  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "The test named for the never-join rule, TestReviewWithABriefNeverJoins in internal/goal/branch, cannot catch the mutation the brief lists for it ('pass --join with FILE'). It calls RunBranchRead directly and never sets Join. The --join decision is made one layer up, in the command (reviewUnitRound). The rule is still guarded: TestReviewOfABuiltUnitTakesACorrectedBrief in cmd/metasystem fails outright if a request with --brief carries --join. The renamed test's doc comment also still names the old test (TestBranchReadRefusedDispatchBindsNothing). Not material: the behaviour works, and another green test pins it.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read_test.go:811-815 has the old comment name and no Join field in the request at :833-835. The guard is metasystem/cmd/metasystem/intent_corrected_brief_test.go:138-140 (t.Fatal on '--join'). The --join choice is in metasystem/cmd/metasystem/intent_unit_review.go:302-307.",
      "id": "F-1",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The frozen-section exemption is keyed on a literal heading line anywhere in a brief that names a reviewed commit. A corrected FILE that itself contains the line '# Supplied accepted implementation brief (frozen at dispatch)' therefore gets the rest of its text exempted. That could happen if an operator hands in a copy of an earlier composed critic brief as the correction. In that case, citations under the Corrected heading after that line are not checked. This goes against the round-1 brief's 'every corrected brief is checked in full'. Not material: it needs an unusual operator input, the worst outcome is a critic citing a file it cannot read (the check that existed before this goal), and the brief itself defines the skip by the heading line.",
      "evidence": "Traced path: metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read.go:313-319 appends FILE verbatim under '# Corrected implementation brief (given at review)'. Then metasystem/internal/dispatch/brief.go:575-583 cuts the text at the first line equal to the frozen heading, wherever it sits, so the lines after it inside FILE are never passed to extractBriefAuthorityPaths.",
      "id": "F-2",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Units whose round was built before this change have no recorded digest. Their own build brief is therefore quoted under the Corrected heading and checked in full at review. Under the old bypass (buildBriefAdmitted plus the record's BriefFromBuild mark), the --work form admitted them. This change removes the bypass, so a legacy unit whose build brief cites a runtime-created file is refused again. The frozen brief explicitly decides this ('A round recorded before this change has no digest'; 'no recorded digest' means the Corrected heading). It is recorded so the coordinator knows that in-flight units built before this change are not helped.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/internal/launch/unit_run.go:337 records a digest only when the first build step has not launched. metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read.go:316 requires a non-empty digest for the frozen heading. metasystem/internal/delegation/admission.go:612-624 has no bypass left.",
      "id": "F-3",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Besides removing the bypass, briefAuthority now routes every brief-authority Git call, for all roles, through the session's Git port with its own timeout, instead of dispatch's direct git calls. The round's list does not name this, but it lets the delegation tests run without real Git, as the constraints require. The commands, the timeout setting and the result handling are equivalent, so I found no behaviour change.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/internal/delegation/admission.go:612-624 compared with metasystem/internal/dispatch/gitcmd.go:19-62. metasystem/internal/dispatch/brief.go:536-566 gets the same argv through gitBriefTreeFacts.output. metasystem/internal/delegation/owners.go:467-477 shows the port runs 'git -C dir'.",
      "id": "F-4",
      "material": false,
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Some text is now stale. The doc comment of TestBuildBriefAdmittedRefusesTheCommitFormsBrief and the matrix's workAdmitted comment ('A person's brief to the review of a commit still is [checked]') no longer hold in general: the commit form now marks and exempts a brief whose bytes match the build's digest. Nothing tests that commit-form case end to end, because the matrix's commit rows were switched to a different brief file. branch.BuildBriefAdmitted no longer has a production caller. These are cosmetic and coverage observations; behaviour is as the brief specifies.",
      "evidence": "metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read_build_brief_test.go:91-93. metasystem/cmd/metasystem/review_start_matrix_test.go:31-33 and :327. metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read.go:153 (the only remaining callers are tests). metasystem/internal/goal/branch/read.go:767 marks BriefFromBuild by digest for any form.",
